<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi> command attempts to sweep your opponent's legs out from under them,
knocking them to the ground. This is primarily a tactical move rather than a damaging attack.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>
  Attempt to trip your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> 25% of your Strength (low damage, tactical move)
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown Chance:</ansi> 60% base (highest of all special moves)
    - Attacker: Unarmed Combat skill + Dexterity
    - Defender: Combat skill + Dexterity
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> 5 rounds (shared with bash and kick)
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Trip has the highest knockdown chance of all special moves, making it ideal for setting
up your allies' attacks. If successful, your target becomes <ansi fg="red">prone</ansi> for a minimum
of 1 full round. See <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi> for details on prone effects.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help stand</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>
